      "name": "Cunning Stunts",
      "description": "Complete 250 Stunts.",
      "grade": "silver",
      "guide": "Cunning Stunts is the silver trophy for landing two hundred and fifty stunts. PlayStation tracks the tally as a single counter, so distance and variety do not change the number: what matters is completing a recognised stunt and landing it cleanly. The efficient method is to pick an area with repeated ramps, a long straight approach and enough open space to absorb a bad landing, then chain attempts without driving back to the start of the map. Mix in a few different stunt types if the counter appears to stall, because some attempts are only registered once the game has classified them. A failed landing does not count, so reset the vehicle when it is badly damaged rather than limping to the next ramp. Keep the radio off and watch the counter in the pause screen every twenty attempts; that rhythm makes a long grind much easier to estimate and keeps the tracker's count honest.",
