      "description": "Try each type of activity once.",
      "grade": "bronze",
      "guide": "Master of None asks you to try each type of activity once. It is a discovery trophy rather than a mastery trophy: you do not need a high score, only a completed attempt of every category the game lists. The reliable way to approach it is to open the map, filter for activity icons and tick them off one by one, using the same order each time so nothing is missed. Some categories are only unlocked after a chapter introduces them, so if the map shows fewer types than you expect, return after the campaign. When you start an activity, stay until the results screen even if the score is poor; abandoning it midway may not mark the type as attempted. Because this sits in the activities part of the list it is never masked by spoiler mode, and it is a good early target when you want to make visible progress without touching story content.",
