      "description": "Earn a gold medal in all Shooting Range challenges.",
      "grade": "silver",
      "guide": "The Shootist is a silver trophy for earning a gold medal in every Shooting Range challenge. There are forty-two challenges in the set, and PlayStation tracks them as individual entries, so the ledger counts them one by one rather than as a single percentage. The practical approach is to work through the range menu in order: each challenge has its own medal thresholds, and a gold result needs both accuracy and speed, not just hits. If a challenge refuses to award gold, replay it with a steadier rhythm rather than firing faster; the timing targets reward controlled bursts. Check the range's results list after every session because it shows which medals are still short, and save before leaving so the records persist. This is one of the longer collectible grinds, so spread it across sessions and use the Collectibles view to see the required count whenever you come back to it.",
