      "id": 20,
      "name": "Baited My Tackle",
      "description": "Beat Cal in a fishing challenge.",
      "grade": "bronze",
      "guide": "Baited My Tackle is awarded for beating Cal in a fishing challenge. This is a small, self-contained activity, but it is easy to overlook because the fishing spots do not shout for attention on the map. Start by locating Cal through the activity list or by checking the shoreline locations the game marks for fishing, then accept the challenge rather than simply casting at random. The contest is about choosing the right bait and landing the fish cleanly; a heavy fish will fight back, so keep the line tension in the safe band instead of reeling constantly. If you lose the round, challenge again rather than leaving the area, because the opponent is fixed to that spot and might not be available later in the day cycle. The trophy pops on the results screen. It is a good target early in the Misc stage because it takes minutes and does not depend on story progress.",
