      "id": 21,
      "name": "Stick Fiddler",
      "description": "Complete an arcade game.",
      "grade": "bronze",
      "guide": "Stick Fiddler asks for a completed arcade game. The game tracks this as a single flag: playing several cabinets partway does not help, while finishing one cabinet from start to finish does. Look for arcade machines inside the city's entertainment venues; they are usually clustered, so once you find one location you can try several machines in the same visit. Pick a simple cabinet with a short loop rather than the most visually impressive one, and use continue options if they are offered. The trophy triggers on the high-score or game-over screen once the cabinet's objective is satisfied, so do not walk away during the final stage. If a machine seems impossible, leave it and try the next cabinet in the same room. Because this is a collectible-style activity with no story content, it remains visible when spoiler mode is switched on, making it a convenient early tick.",
