      "id": 29,
      "name": "Fair Game",
      "description": "Hunt a unique animal for Bret.",
      "grade": "bronze",
      "guide": "Fair Game is earned by hunting a unique animal for Bret. This is a single objective hidden inside the hunting activity rather than a general hunting count, so random kills will not satisfy it. Start by speaking with Bret to learn which animal he wants, then check the map for the highlighted habitat and travel there at the right time of day if the game specifies one. Use a suitable weapon and approach from downwind; a clean shot is preferable to a long chase because the animal can flee and reset. Once the animal is harvested, return to Bret to hand in the request. The trophy registers on the hand-in, not on the kill, so do not tick the row early. This entry is classed with collectibles because it is a fixed, one-off discovery target. It also tends to unlock nearby hunting challenges, so it is worth doing before you sweep the rest of the region.",
